     "<div dir=\"ltr\">You can use tidyverse and broom to return a data frame with all of the output from the t.test for each model. For example:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">tidyverse</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">broom</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">test_results </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> map2_df</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">df1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> df2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\">tidy</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">test</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">id</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Model&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><br><br><br><br>On Thursday, June 15, 2017 at 7:48:13 AM UTC-7, bic ton wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<div><br></div><div>I have two data.frames   dt1  dt2 </div><div><br></div><div><div>&gt; str(dt1)</div><div>&#39;data.frame&#39;:   377 obs. of  10 variables:</div><div> $ ACC      : num   23 6 1 4 ...</div><div> $ ES      : num   213 6 4  ...</div><div> $ bcc   : num   23 6 1 4 ..</div></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><div>&gt; str(dt2)</div><div>&#39;data.frame&#39;:   377 obs. of  10 variables:</div><div> $ ACC      : num  5 2 3 6 2</div><div> $ ES      : num  25 1 3 6 </div><div> $ bcc   : num   2 1 5 4 6 9 ..</div></div><div><br></div><div>In each data.frame I have 10 models. I want to apply t.test for each model to compare the means for example:</div><div>t.test(dt1$ACC,dt2$ACC)p.value</div><div><br></div><div>How to do this for all models instead of typing this 10 times?</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks</div><div>Bic</div></div></blockquote></div>"
